        +'<h3>Bonuses &amp; promotions on game shows</h3><p>Every game-show bet earns VIP rakeback and counts toward the $100,000 Weekly Race and the $75,000 Raffle, exactly like the instant games. Launch-week shows will carry boosted-multiplier events of their own — join from the Promotions page so you do not miss the first drop.</p>'+secBtn("promos","See Promotions")+'</div>'
        +'</div>'
        +'<div class="gs-article" id="gsMore">'
        +'<div><h3>How RTP and house edge work in game shows</h3><p>Game shows trade a little RTP for spectacle: the bonus rounds are funded by slightly lower base-game returns, so most titles sit between 94% and 97% RTP depending on which segments you back. Backing only the numbers is the low-variance route; the bonus segments pay rarely, but enormously.</p>'
        +'<h3>How to play — your first show</h3><ul><li><b>Pick a show</b> and watch a round or two to learn its rhythm.</li><li><b>Place your bet</b> on a number, colour or bonus segment before the timer ends.</li><li><b>Ride the bonus</b> — if your segment hits, the host plays the bonus round for everyone on it.</li><li><b>Get paid automatically</b> the second the round settles, multipliers included.</li></ul>'
        +'<h3>Beginners vs high rollers</h3><p>New to the floor? Mega Wheel and Football Studio are the gentlest starts — simple bets and frequent small wins. Chasing the ceiling? Crazy Time and Lightning Storm carry the biggest multipliers, and the VIP salon tables open with limits up to $100,000.</p></div>'
        +'<div><h3>Inside Crazy Time — the four bonus rounds</h3><ul><li><b>Coin Flip</b> — a red-and-blue coin flip with multipliers generated live.</li><li><b>Cash Hunt</b> — a shooting gallery of 108 hidden multipliers; pick your target.</li><li><b>Pachinko</b> — a puck drops down a peg wall into multiplier slots, with doubles that trigger a re-drop.</li><li><b>Crazy Time</b> — the door to a giant virtual wheel with multipliers up to 20,000×.</li></ul><p>A top-slot multiplier is drawn before every spin and applied to one bonus segment — which is how a good round becomes a legendary one.</p>'
